# HTTP headers for the deployed site. The same format is read by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify
# (a path line, then indented "Name: value" lines). `astro preview` and `pnpm dev` ignore this
# file, so it only takes effect on the host. See "Deploy" in README.md.
#
# The Content Security Policy for scripts and styles is NOT here: it carries a hash for every
# script and style of a build, so Astro writes it into a <meta> tag on every page
# (`security.csp` in astro.config.mjs). Only what a <meta> tag cannot express is set here.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

# The service worker must always be revalidated, or an update could wait behind the HTTP cache
# (browsers already bypass it for the worker script, this makes it explicit for every host).
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Files under /_astro/ have a content hash in their name, so they never change.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
